  "text": "The provided code is a Verilog-2001 module interface for an asynchronous AXI-Stream FIFO. It includes parameters for the depth, data width, keep enable, keep width, last enable, id enable, id width, dest enable, dest width, user enable, user width, ram pipeline, output fifo enable, frame fifo, user bad frame value, user bad frame mask, drop oversize frame, drop bad frame, drop when full, mark when full, pause enable, and frame pause.\n\nThe module has inputs for the AXI input (s_clk, s_rst, s_axis_tdata, s_axis_tkeep, s_axis_tvalid, s_axis_tlast, s_axis_tid, s_axis_tdest, s_axis_tuser), AXI output (m_clk, m_rst, m_axis_tdata, m_axis_tkeep, m_axis_tvalid, m_axis_tlast, m_axis_tid, m_axis_tdest, m_axis_tuser), pause (s_pause_req, m_pause_req), and status (s_status_depth, s_status_depth_commit, s_status_overflow, s_status_bad_frame, s_status_good_frame, m_status_depth, m_status_depth_commit, m_status_overflow, m_status_bad_frame, m_status_good_frame).\n\nThe module does not include any Verilog code for the actual implementation of the FIFO. The complete Verilog-2001 code for the module would need to be provided by the module designer.\n<|EOT|>",
